  memory_rw              measures stack   pin: yes

  1 of 14 differentials measure stack by the known idiom
  BLINDNESS, printed every run: this detects the STACK-WATERMARK idiom ONLY.
  An allocation counter, an iteration count, a timing loop, or a future stack
  idiom would all slip past.  A green line means 'no UNPINNED file uses the shape
  that has actually bitten' -- NEVER 'no row follows the compiler'.
OPTPIN_PASS  every resource-measuring differential pins its optimisation
